    {
      "id": 241799,
      "name": "FrivYeti",
      "username": "FrivYeti",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-12-29T17:37:31.895Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint!</p>\n<p>I almost killed myself pretty handily when, with an Explosives Wagon out, Legacy opened all of his presents from Guise and flipped Surge of Strength and then <em>three</em> Heroic Interceptions, dealing himself fifteen damage.</p>\n<p>I can’t imagine what Legacy did to earn that pile of coal.</p>\n<p>But I still pulled it together, and finished the game with everyone still standing. Fanatic and Legacy were well into the single digits, but Guise and Adept were both in the high teens, so I probably would have been fine even with a couple more bad pulls.</p>\n<p>Interesting thing that I discovered, and probably should have recognized: if Guise steals the Adept’s instrument, he can activate songs in the Argent Adept’s play area, but those songs affect the Adept, not Guise. The rewrite effect on stolen equipment only covers the instrument itself, not any abilities it activates.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-12-29T17:37:31.895Z",
      "reply_count": 1,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 19,
      "readers_count": 18,
      "score": 38.8,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 28994,
      "topic_slug": "weekly-one-shot-315-wrapping-with-guise",
      "display_username": "FrivYeti",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Mint!\n\nI almost killed myself pretty handily when, with an Explosives Wagon out, Legacy opened all of his presents from Guise and flipped Surge of Strength and then *three* Heroic Interceptions, dealing himself fifteen damage. \n\nI can't imagine what Legacy did to earn that pile of coal.\n\nBut I still pulled it together, and finished the game with everyone still standing. Fanatic and Legacy were well into the single digits, but Guise and Adept were both in the high teens, so I probably would have been fine even with a couple more bad pulls.\n\nInteresting thing that I discovered, and probably should have recognized: if Guise steals the Adept's instrument, he can activate songs in the Argent Adept's play area, but those songs affect the Adept, not Guise. The rewrite effect on stolen equipment only covers the instrument itself, not any abilities it activates.",
      "actions_summary": [
        {
          "id": 2,
          "count": 2,
          "can_act": true
        },
